12:09:04 said  **Found the root bug.** The camera position formula mixes azimuth conventions: `x += sin(az)`, `z += cos(az)` treats `az` as an angle from +Z, but everything else uses atan2(z,x) azimuths. With `az = heading + π + yaw` the camera ended up ~104° off the boat's stern instead of behind it — that's why the view pointed 20° instead of 67°. Fix:
